WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.520
Jabba the Hutt isn't just a crime boss, as
far as the Star Wars universe is concerned,

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.980
he is the boss.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.340
But Jabba is so much more than just a lazy,
corrupt blob.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.469
He's got a history that's just as gross and
bizarre as his slime-coated skin.

00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:16.860
Here are a few things you might not know about

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.160
Jabba Desilijic Tiure...

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:19.790
Jabba Desilijic Tiure…

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:25.970
Jabba Desigurbearear...

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.470
Jabba the Hutt.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.579
A slimy evolution

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:33.680
Jabba the Hutt is famous for his bulbous body
and slug-like features.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.880
In the decades since his debut in Return of
the Jedi, he's become a symbol for gluttony

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.030
and corruption, and it's all thanks to his
disgusting, pulsating bod.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.430
But Jabba could have looked very different.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:49.200
In the original Star Wars script, he's simply
ambiguously described big and gross, with

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.450
facial scars from vicious battles.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.910
In the original concept art, he's vaguely
Chewbacca-like and stands on two legs, and

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:00.640
in the Marvel Comics Star Wars adaptation,
he's a yellow humanoid with a snout and bushy

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.100
mutton chops.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.909
It was only when Return of the Jedi entered
pre-production that Jabba started to take

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:07.690
his now-familiar form.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:12.200
But bringing a giant, slug-like Jabba to life
was a major production.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.920
In Return of the Jedi, there were three main
puppeteers, and other performers moved his

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.760
eyes and helped animate his tail.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.640
Larry Ward, who also voiced Greedo, provided
the vocals.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.850
Over the years, a lot of people have played
Jabba.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.140
Declan Mulholland played the first, weirdly
human Jabba the Hutt in a scene that was ultimately

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.310
cut from the original Star Wars.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:35.150
Veteran actor Ed Asner played Jabba in a radio
drama, and in The Clone Wars, he's played

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:37.100
by Kevin Michael Richardson.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.920
Several different actors have voiced him in
video games.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:43.590
And in The Phantom Menace, he's credited as
being played by "himself."

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.140
Figure that one out.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.270
Mommy issues

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:51.220
Jabba is a mobster from a family of mobsters,
so of course his family reunions get a little

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.220
complicated.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:57.740
In 2008, the animated film The Clone Wars
introduced Jabba's uncle, Ziro the Hutt, and

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.770
his son, the flatulent Rotta.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:04.700
Later, the cartoon series expanded Jabba's
family tree by bringing in other family members,

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.250
including the obese Hutt matriarch Mama.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:11.870
Jabba's parents don't play a big on-screen
role, although they clearly had an impact

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.200
on the young Hutt.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.989
According to The Star Wars Character Encyclopedia,
one of Jabba's dancers, Yarna d'al' Gargan,

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:20.879
was made in his mother's image.

00:02:20.879 --> 00:02:23.840
If she seems a little Hutt-like, that's not
an accident.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.440
As the Character Encyclopedia explains, Jabba
had Yarna's body "enlarged" and forces her

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.819
to wear makeup that makes her look like his
mom.

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:33.719
Yes, it's all a little weird, even for Jabba.

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:37.549
Still, twisted parent-kid relationships are
kind of a Star Wars thing, and it wouldn't

00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:41.749
be the first time we've seen characters in
a galaxy far, far away getting a little too

00:02:41.749 --> 00:02:43.900
close to their family members.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.680
How to speak Hutt

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:49.190
You can't actually learn Huttese, because
it's not a real language.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.670
It is, however, based on one.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.340
On the DVD commentary track for A New Hope,
Lucasfilm sound designer Ben Burtt says he

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.950
based Huttese on Quechua, a collection of
loosely affiliated South American languages

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.420
that date back to ancient Incan times.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.040
As the story goes, Burtt located an instructional
tape and played it for Larry Ward, who used

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.449
the sounds to create Huttese words for Jabba.

00:03:10.449 --> 00:03:14.379
Huttese isn't actually Quechua, it has no
formal structure.

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:18.349
Not that anyone on set would've noticed: During
filming, Jabba's puppeteers delivered all

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:19.529
his lines in English.

00:03:19.529 --> 00:03:23.799
The Huttese was added in post-production,
and it was designed to fit Jabba's already-filmed

00:03:23.799 --> 00:03:24.799
mouth movements.

00:03:24.799 --> 00:03:31.150
"Your mind powers will not work on me boy!"

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:32.840
Dude looks like a lady

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.939
Hutt physiology is really freakin' weird.

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:40.019
According to reference books like The New
Essential Guide to Alien Species, Hutts don't

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:44.670
have skeletons, although they do have a "mantle"
that helps give their heads that distinct,

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.670
blobby shape.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:49.529
They sweat mucus, and they have snake-like
qualities, too.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:54.909
In the 1995 comic Jabba the Hutt: The Dynasty
Trap, Jabba is seen swallowing an entire human.

00:03:54.909 --> 00:03:58.419
And while Jabba has a son, don't go looking
for Mrs. Hutt.

00:03:58.419 --> 00:03:59.739
She doesn't exist.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:04.549
In Star Wars' old continuity, Hutts were born
with both male and female reproductive organs,

00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:07.010
and could choose to mate with themselves.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.479
According to the novelization of Star Wars:
The Clone Wars, that's exactly what Jabba

00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:12.479
did.

00:04:12.479 --> 00:04:17.850
In 2012, though, after Disney purchased Lucasfilm,
the Mouse House wiped most of Star Wars' non-film

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:19.450
continuity clean.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.910
As part of this reshuffling, the Hutts got
definitive genders.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.230
Jabba's hermaphroditic past is gone.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.110
For better or worse, he's now a dude, and
only a dude.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:30.400
Tats for Hutts

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.130
Jabba's arm tattoo wasn't supposed to be important.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.940
It was supposed to look cool.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:39.560
In an interview with ScifiNow, John Coppinger,
the man who sculpted Jabba, said the tattoo

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.400
was really just a meaningless afterthought.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.930
"I put a tattoo onto Jabba's arm, as a finishing
touch.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.980
[...] Now if you Google 'Jabba Tattoo' there
you'll find yards of information about Huttese

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.390
tribal markings."

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:54.860
In the novel Darth Plagueis, Jabba's tattoo
is implied to be the symbol of his clan, a

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:59.270
crime family known just as much for their
fearsome loyalty as for their greed, their

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.520
opulent tastes, and their fondness for humanoid
women.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.790
Hey, at least Jabba's comfortable in his own
gross, slimy skin.

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.120
You can't say that about a lot of people.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:14.220
"He doesn't feel the need to be charming,
or anything he's just an unpretentious, very

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:15.220
straightforward, guy."

